|entry[2026-08-06-integrated-delete-test-correction] :date <2026-08-06> :by joseph+claude
  :scope plan/.integrated (emptied), plan/INFLUX (16 files returned), ONTOLOGY
  Steward applied the delete-test and the dispatches failed it: .integrated/ held
  gather-native files whose information was not fully landed, justified by a
  2026-08-05 norm that redefined "integrated" to fit the dispatches. That norm is
  deleted (not softened); replaced by |integrated-is-disposable — the estate law:
  nothing is integrated unless truly disposable or landed; assume it disappears.
  Copies with verified live originals moved to .archive (their honest bucket);
  everything else returned to INFLUX. .integrated is now empty, which is the true
  state: nothing has yet earned it. Steward probes also established the drafted
  layer is ~60% of the notes' claims with the process-law rows (integration SOPs,
  absence, DAG-order) the least covered — and the integration SOPs were never
  gathered at all (added to the named-absence list).

|entry[2026-08-05-influx-batch-integration] :date <2026-08-05> :by claude+5-opus-integrators+sonnet-verifiers+grok
  :scope whole project — INFLUX metabolized, 31 new segments, ONTOLOGY process law
  Five parallel opus integrators (asf+build / udon-analysis+syntheses / tribunal /
  vera / instances+methodology), each with adversarial sonnet verification, drafted
  31 segments and dispatched INFLUX to .integrated/.archive with byte-identity
  verification on every archived copy. Corpus now 48 segments, 85 rows (48 drafted).
  Residue: ~120 items across five registers routed by outline row. Remaining in
  INFLUX by deliberate judgment: live-state-field-reports + deployments (still
  residue-bearing), the ennaos VERA pair (reserved for the joint session), this
  index. Cross-chunk fixes applied at adjudication: gate-is-procedural calibration
  on [[verification-provenance]]; V18 honest reword of [[confidence-calibration]]'s
  row; MOVED→firmatum path repointing (C1); [[proxy-discipline]] row added
  (practiced-but-unlegislated). ONTOLOGY gained four earned norms from the batch:
  parallel-batch-law (slug creation is the unprotected surface; dep-validity at
  merge; appendices name subjects never consumers), readable-claims-tripwire
  (tables and 3+-counts are appendix-grade — names don't fire, tripwires do),
  provenance-registers (first-hand / live-source / inherited-at-stated-remove),
  integrated-means-remainder-registered. Live pattern results observed during the
  batch itself: complementary convergence under parallel drafting; two new-slug
  near-collisions; a path-rot recurrence during the session documenting path rot;
  a verifier committing V7 while writing the register that carries V7.

|entry[2026-08-05-influx-first-dispatch] :date <2026-08-05> :by claude (fresh-eyes agent)
  :scope plan/INFLUX + plan/.archive + plan/.integrated + four segments' Working Notes
  First metabolism pass on INFLUX: segments read first, then the overlapping notes, then
  residue reported. Dispatched 9 of ~80 files. To .archive/: the seven `udon-theory/`
  copies and `primary/cross-corpus-generalization-2026-07-23.md` — each **verified
  byte-identical** to its live original (`MOVED/udon/v2/theory/`,
  `arch/notes/outline-segments-generalization-2026-07-23.md`), so archive-shaped by
  construction; the live corpora are the citable landings. To .integrated/:
  `synthesis/scatter-inventory-2026-08-05.md` (map role discharged). Deliberately left in
  INFLUX: `live-state-field-reports` and `instances/deployments.md` — both still carry
  content with no segment home. Residue that no segment carries is registered as R1–R25 in
  plan/INFLUX-DISPATCH-2026-08-05.md, routed by OUTLINE row rather than by source note so
  later dispatches cannot orphan it; INFLUX/00-INDEX.md struck the departed rows.
  Six field-report claims marked (scout) were re-verified first-hand and now hold ✔
  (def-chronica 63% WN; lint-outline's `old-*` exemption; vivarium 0 GAP rows over 115
  segments; asf 03/04 0 GAP rows; neurips-refs 7% vs logos-refs 72% verified; comproprium
  51 unintegrated harvest segments), plus one new measurement: `stage` denormalization
  drift across 01-aat-core is **0 mismatches in 168 comparisons**. Working-Notes residue
  lines appended to [[collision-staleness-detection]], [[turnover-solution]],
  [[substrate-independence]], [[coupling-confounding]] — no segment bodies touched.
  Not examined: asf/, udon-analysis/, tribunal/, vera/, build/, methodology/, most of
  instances/.

